Step 1 — Setup
git checkout develop
cd 2026b-cosc2767-a1-<repo-name>
mkdir question-3
cd question-3
curl -L -O https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TomHuynhSG/public_datasets/refs/heads/master/app_server_2026.log

Before writing any pipelines, inspect the actual file first — CSV files sometimes quote fields ("401" instead of 401), which changes your awk match:

head -5 app_server_2026.log

Adjust the commands below if you see quotes around values — I'll note the fix either way.

Field reference (from the format line given)
1=Timestamp, 2=IP_Address, 3=UserID, 4=HTTP_Status, 5=HTTP_Method, 6=User_Agent, 7=Request_URI, 8=Response_Size

Task 2 — Auth errors (401/403) → screenshot 3a.png
awk -F',' '$4 == "401" || $4 == "403"' app_server_2026.log > authentication_errors.log
cat authentication_errors.log

Screenshot both the command and the cat output together.

If head showed quoted values (e.g. ..., "401", ...), use this:
awk -F',' '$4 == "\"401\"" || $4 == "\"403\""' app_server_2026.log > authentication_errors.log

Task 3 — Top 3 IPs by request count → screenshot 3b.png
echo "Top 3 IP addresses:"
awk -F',' 'NR>1 {print $2}' app_server_2026.log | sort | uniq -c | sort -nr | head -3
NR>1 skips the header row (remove it if the file has no header line — check your head -5 output).
$2 = IP_Address field.
sort | uniq -c groups and counts identical IPs; sort -nr orders by count descending; head -3 keeps only the top three — matching the count IP output format shown in the question exactly.

Task 4 — Top 5 requested URIs
echo "Top 5 request URIs:"
awk -F',' 'NR>1 {print $7}' app_server_2026.log | sort | uniq -c | sort -nr | head -5

Same pipeline pattern, just swapping $2 (IP) for $7 (Request_URI) and head -3 for head -5.

